ABAP RAP Learning Notes
=======================

1. Core RAP Development Flow
----------------------------
The foundational pipeline for exposing data in the ABAP RESTful Application Programming Model:

Interface View (I-View) -> Projection View (C-View) -> Service Definition -> Service Binding


2. Semantically Dependent Elements
----------------------------------
Used to link quantities or amounts to their corresponding units or currencies.

@Semantics.quantity.unitOfMeasure: 'UnitField'
element_qty;

@Semantics.amount.currencyCode: 'CurrencyField'
element_amt;


3. UI Annotations (List Reports & Object Pages)
-----------------------------------------------
General UI Elements:
* @UI.headerInfo: Defines the header details (title, description, types) on the Object Page.
* Selection Fields: The filter bar at the top of a List Report.
* Search: Global search capability.
* Value Help: F4 input help configuration.

Syntax Breakdown:
// Defines row position in the List Report grid (relative positioning)
@UI.lineItem: [{ position: 10, label: 'New Label' }] 

// Exposes the field as a filter criteria in the selection bar
@UI.selectionField: [{ position: 10 }] 

// Defines the position and label inside the Object Page's identification block
@UI.identification: [{ position: 10, label: 'Field Label' }] 

TIP: You can change or save default UI layouts using Variants directly in the UI launchpad.


4. UI Facets (Object Page Layout)
---------------------------------
Facets define the structural layout of your Object Page to display detailed information in sections or tabs.

@UI.facet: [
  {
    id:          'Id1',
    purpose:     #STANDARD,
    type:        #IDENTIFICATION_REFERENCE,
    position:    10,
    label:       'General Information'
  },
  {
    id:           'Id2',
    purpose:      #STANDARD,
    type:         #LINEITEM_REFERENCE,
    position:     20,
    label:        'Items List',
    targetElement: '_AssociationCDS' // Target association must be exposed in the Service Definition
  }
]


5. CDS Associations
-------------------
Used to define relationships between data models.

association [1..*] to zcds_target_view as _AssociationName 
  on $projection.field1 = _AssociationName.field2

Text Associations:
To automatically fetch and display text descriptions from a text provider CDS view:

1. In the main view:
   @ObjectModel.text.association: '_TextAssociation'
   element_id;

2. In the target text view (_TextAssociation):
   @Semantics.text: true
   element_text;


6. Search Capabilities
----------------------
To enable text search fields in your application:

@Search.searchable: true // Placed at the header level of the CDS View

// Inside the element list:
@Search.defaultSearchElement: true
@Search.fuzzinessThreshold: 0.8
element_name;

Search via Associations (Object Page Search):
To make child/associated entities searchable from the root/main CDS:
* Set @Search.defaultSearchElement: true on the association alias in the main view.
* Ensure the child CDS view is marked @Search.searchable: true at its header level, and its text/key fields have @Search.defaultSearchElement: true.


7. Value Helps (F4 Help)
------------------------
Binds an elementary field to a search help data source.

@Consumption.valueHelpDefinition: [{ 
  entity: { name: 'ZCDS_VALUE_HELP_VIEW', element: 'TargetField' } 
}]
element_id;

8.Sortby in cds -> Cannot be done using order by clause.Can be achieved using UI Annotation.

@UI.presentationVariant: [{
    sortOrder: [
        { by: 'Country', direction: #ASC } 
    ],
    visualizations: [{ type: #AS_LINEITEM }]
}]


8. Developer Quick Tip
----------------------
Verifying Active Annotations: To check the final evaluated annotations (including inherited ones) for your CDS view: 
* Right-click inside your CDS code editor -> select Open With -> Active Annotations.
